---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config.mjs';

const updated = '8 September 2026';
const mail = SITE.contactEmail;
---

<Layout
  title={`Terms of Use — ${SITE.name}`}
  description="The terms for using this site: what you may do with it, what we do and do not promise about products and prices, and who you are actually buying from."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-bold text-ink">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose prose-sm mt-8 max-w-none text-muted prose-headings:font-serif prose-headings:text-ink prose-strong:text-ink prose-a:text-terracotta">
      <p class="lead">
        Short version: read anything you like, buy nothing from us, and check the price on Amazon
        before you buy anything there. The rest is detail.
      </p>

      <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} is published by an independent publisher based in Slovenia, in the European
        Union. Contact for anything on this page:
        {mail
          ? <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>
          : <mark class="rounded bg-terracotta/15 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-terracotta-dark">[ contact email ]</mark>}.
        These details are published because the E-Commerce Directive requires a service provider to
        be identifiable and directly contactable before you deal with it.
      </p>

      <h2>Using the site</h2>
      <p>
        Read it, print it, send a link to whoever is redecorating. You need no permission from us
        for any of that. What you may not do is scrape the whole thing and republish it as your own
        site, or use it in a way that breaks the law or knocks the site over.
      </p>
      <p>
        The written text, the curation and the layout are ours. Product names, product photographs
        and the Amazon marks belong to their respective owners and are used to identify the products
        we are pointing you at.
      </p>

      <h2>We are not the seller</h2>
      <p>
        This is important, so it gets its own heading. Nothing is sold here. Every product link goes
        to Amazon, and any purchase is a contract between you and Amazon or one of its third-party
        sellers. Payment, delivery, warranty, returns and complaints are entirely theirs, and your
        consumer rights on that purchase run against them, not against us.
      </p>

      <h2>Prices, ratings and availability</h2>
      <p>
        We deliberately do not show live prices, because they change hourly and a stale price on a
        blog is worse than none. Ratings and review counts are correct as of the day the page was
        built and drift afterwards. Availability changes constantly. Always check the current price,
        rating and availability on Amazon before buying. Anything here is editorial opinion and
        general information, not advice for your specific situation.
      </p>

      <h2>How we make money</h2>
      <p>
        Through the Amazon Associates programme: if you buy after clicking one of our links, we may
        earn a commission at no extra cost to you. That is set out in full on the
        <a href="/disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a> page, and it is disclosed on every page of
        this site because the law and Amazon both require it. It does not change what we recommend:
        picks are chosen on rating and quality, not on commission.
      </p>

      <h2>The newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        Subscribing is free and voluntary, and every email carries a one-click unsubscribe that
        works. We send the newsletter a few times a week and use the list for nothing else. How your
        email address is handled is in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>. We may stop
        sending it at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        We link to Amazon and occasionally elsewhere. We do not control those sites and are not
        responsible for their content or for what they do with your data once you are there.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability and liability</h2>
      <p>
        We would like the site to be up all the time and it very nearly always is, but we do not
        promise it, and we may change or remove any page without notice. The content is provided as
        it is. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for loss arising from relying on
        information here, from a product bought through a link, or from the site being unavailable.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing in these terms limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence,
        for fraud, or for anything else that cannot lawfully be limited, and nothing here takes away
        the mandatory consumer rights you have under the law of your own country.
      </p>

      <h2>Law and changes</h2>
      <p>
        Slovenian law applies, and if you are a consumer resident elsewhere in the EU you keep the
        protection of the mandatory rules of your own country. We may update these terms; the
        version that applies is the one published when you read the site, and the date at the top
        moves when it changes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
